// Title: Visual Studio NodejsTools PressAnyKey Arbitrary Binary Execution
// Sigma ID: a20391f8-76fb-437b-abc0-dba2df1952c6
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-11 | Modified: 2023-04-11
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects child processes of Microsoft.NodejsTools.PressAnyKey.exe that can be used to execute any
//   other binary
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by developers as part of NodeJS development with Visual Studio Tools
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1463526834918854661
//   - https://gist.github.com/nasbench/a989ce64cefa8081bd50cf6ad8c491b5
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pressanykey_lolbin_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft.NodejsTools.PressAnyKey.exe"
